Our nutrition depends on light as well.  As one of the most common 
examples, we synthesize vitamin D through our skin via ultraviolet 
exposure.  15 minutes a day does the trick, and it does have an effect on 
our moods, if not more.

And although there is almost no 'evidence' from the mainstream medical 
community, light, sound, color, magnetism, and all sorts of forces affect 
the human being.  There is no money in researching this avenues for 
mainstream medicine- you can't patent sunlight.  I don't want to debate 
this points, sorry, I just leave it to say that I believe there are lots 
of things in this universe that we don't understand yet, can not even 
detect, that exist and have effects on us, some of them quite profound.

